check.model:
(1) Student 1 — Make — M Checkout M — Be made for — 1 Book (resolving Student M — Borrow — N Book; both original sides optional). Publisher 1 — Publish — M Book: each book exactly one publisher (mandatory, 1); each publisher one or more books (mandatory, M). Checkout dates are attributes of the associative entity Checkout.

(2)
CREATE TABLE STUDENT (SID CHAR(5) PRIMARY KEY, SNAME VARCHAR(20));
CREATE TABLE PUBLISHER (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30));
CREATE TABLE BOOK (BID INT PRIMARY KEY, TITLE VARCHAR(50), PID INT NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PUBLISHER(PID));
CREATE TABLE CHECKOUT (SID CHAR(5), BID INT, CDATE DATE, DDATE DATE, RDATE DATE,
  PRIMARY KEY (SID, BID, CDATE),
  FOREIGN KEY (SID) REFERENCES STUDENT(SID),
  FOREIGN KEY (BID) REFERENCES BOOK(BID));

Key points: CDATE is part of the key because the same student can borrow the same book again; RDATE may be NULL until returned; the FK for the 1:M relationship goes in BOOK.

pr.solution:
CREATE TABLE STUDENT (SID CHAR(5) PRIMARY KEY, SNAME VARCHAR(20));
CREATE TABLE PUBLISHER (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30));
CREATE TABLE BOOK (BID INT PRIMARY KEY, TITLE VARCHAR(50), PID INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PUBLISHER(PID));
CREATE TABLE CHECKOUT (SID CHAR(5), BID INT, CDATE DATE, DDATE DATE, RDATE DATE, PRIMARY KEY (SID, BID, CDATE), FOREIGN KEY (SID) REFERENCES STUDENT(SID), FOREIGN KEY (BID) REFERENCES BOOK(BID));

check.model:
(1) OID → {ODATE, CID}; CID → {CNAME, CPHONE}; PID → {PNAME, UNITPRICE}; {OID, PID} → QTY.
Not 2NF: ODATE, CID depend only on OID and PNAME, UNITPRICE only on PID (partial dependencies on part of the composite key).
Not 3NF: after splitting, ORDERS(OID, ODATE, CID, CNAME, CPHONE) has OID → CID → {CNAME, CPHONE}, a transitive dependency.

(2)
CREATE TABLE CUSTOMER (CID INT PRIMARY KEY, CNAME VARCHAR(30), CPHONE CHAR(8));
CREATE TABLE PRODUCT (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30), UNITPRICE DECIMAL(8,2));
CREATE TABLE ORDERS (OID INT PRIMARY KEY, ODATE DATE, CID INT NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (CID) REFERENCES CUSTOMER(CID));
CREATE TABLE ORDERITEM (OID INT, PID INT, QTY INT, PRIMARY KEY (OID, PID),
  FOREIGN KEY (OID) REFERENCES ORDERS(OID),
  FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PRODUCT(PID));

pr.solution:
CREATE TABLE CUSTOMER (CID INT PRIMARY KEY, CNAME VARCHAR(30), CPHONE CHAR(8));
CREATE TABLE PRODUCT (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30), UNITPRICE DECIMAL(8,2));
CREATE TABLE ORDERS (OID INT PRIMARY KEY, ODATE DATE, CID INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY (CID) REFERENCES CUSTOMER(CID));
CREATE TABLE ORDERITEM (OID INT, PID INT, QTY INT, PRIMARY KEY (OID, PID), FOREIGN KEY (OID) REFERENCES ORDERS(OID), FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PRODUCT(PID));
